{"name":"Dill Pickle","hex":"#67744a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dill pickle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cucumber pickled in brine or vinegar flavored with dill and other seasonings.","A foolish person. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dill_pickle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickled cucumber","blocks":[{"text":"A pickled cucumber – commonly known as a pickle in the United States and Canada and a gherkin in Britain, Ireland, South Africa, Australia and New Zealand – is a usually small or miniature cucumber that has been pickled in a brine, vinegar, or other solution and left to ferment. The fermentation process is executed either by immersing the cucumbers in an acidic solution or through souring by lacto-fermentation. Pickled cucumbers are often part of mixed pickles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Pickle.jpg/330px-Pickle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickled_cucumber"},{"title":"Dill","blocks":[{"text":"Dill is an annual herb in the celery family Apiaceae. Native to North Africa and West Asia, dill is grown widely in Eurasia, where its leaves and seeds are used as a herb or spice for flavouring food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Illustration_Anethum_graveolens_clean.jpg/330px-Illustration_Anethum_graveolens_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dill"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Pickled_cucumber.jpg/500px-Pickled_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Pickled_cucumber.jpg/500px-Pickled_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai